# CODEOWNERS — example. Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and adapt.
#
# NOTE FOR SOLO / CONSTRAINED TEAMS:
# CODEOWNERS with require_code_owner_reviews and one engineer = nothing ever merges.
# Use it WITHOUT the required-review setting: it still routes review requests, still
# documents ownership, and still marks which paths are consequential — without
# creating a self-blocking gate. Turn the requirement on when a second qualified
# reviewer exists.

# Default
*                               @your-org/engineering

# ---- Consequential paths: these define the "invariant-adjacent" surface -----
# Even unenforced, listing them here documents WHERE independent challenge matters.

/.github/workflows/             @your-org/platform @your-org/security
/.github/actions/               @your-org/platform
/developer-safety/              @your-org/security
/infra/                         @your-org/platform
/**/*.tf                        @your-org/platform
/**/Dockerfile*                 @your-org/platform

# Auth, identity, data model, audit — highest independent-review value
/**/auth/                       @your-org/security
/**/rbac/                       @your-org/security
/**/migrations/                 @your-org/data
/**/audit/                      @your-org/security
/schemas/                       @your-org/architecture

# Policy and governance
/policy/                        @your-org/security
/docs/decisions/                @your-org/architecture
